  "channel": "stable",
  "notes": "- **Security fix for CVE-2026-111497.** The Brotli decompression library the\n  browser uses to unpack web pages could be made to write past the end of\n  its memory by a malicious server. This update brings the fixed library\n  (Debian's 1.1.0-2+deb13u1) to every display through the normal software\n  update, without an operating system update, and the browser restarts in\n  the maintenance window to start using it. Once a display later gets an\n  operating system update that already contains the fix, this copy removes\n  itself.\n- **The Updates card no longer asks you to install an older release.** A\n  display running a newer version than its channel publishes showed \"Waiting\n  to install\" for the older release, although it would never install it.\n  Nothing was ever downgraded; the line was only wrong.\n- **The security fix now takes effect in the same update that delivers it.**\n  Before, the fixed library was put in place but only switched on by the next\n  hourly check.",
  "notes_covers": ["1.15.28.2", "1.15.28.1", "1.15.28.3"],
